config AMLOGIC_ADLA_COMPAT
	tristate "Amlogic T7C ADLA downstream SDK compatibility"
	depends on ARM64 && OF && ARCH_MESON
	depends on PM && REGULATOR
	help
	  Downstream compatibility interface for the Amlogic ADLA SDK.
	  Exposes /dev/adla0 and the vendor ioctl, mmap and sysfs contracts.
	  This is not a DRM accelerator interface. Hardware validation is
	  required before use on T7C boards.

config AMLOGIC_ADLA_KUNIT_TEST
	tristate "KUnit tests for ADLA memory and cancellation" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on KUNIT && AMLOGIC_ADLA_COMPAT
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Test the production bitmap allocator, queued cancellation and
	  untrusted command bounds using real driver types and kernel lists.
	  DMA, recovery, power and ioctl lifetimes require board validation.
	  This suite may also be built as a separate KUnit module.
